                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2bdee422-0d20-3eca-9974-75d3afe4fca1",
                        "entry_id": "80457b3b-549f-3f0d-87c2-10d1415dcbb1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An exchange that takes place beforehand."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ce5bd8c-a9a5-43e5-a4de-46ed91ed95df",
                                "sense_id": "2bdee422-0d20-3eca-9974-75d3afe4fca1",
                                "text": "The solicitor acting for the vendor in one of these cases had cause to telephone the writer this afternoon to request an early date for exchange of contracts, and, upon being advised of the horror with which the writer had viewed the above clause, advised that she quite agreed with the views expressed, to whit that such a clause made mockery of the whole question of preexchange of contract enquiries, but said that this clause was now put into virtually all contracts prepared by Kent solicitors."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23b9763b-3d66-4d14-a9a0-26057b483998",
                                "sense_id": "2bdee422-0d20-3eca-9974-75d3afe4fca1",
                                "text": "On the other hand, one of the most critical concerns in a cryptographic or COMSEC system is that of key management — the method used to effect the necessary preexchange of private information to permit successful intercommunication over an encrypted link."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96842add-ec4b-4868-ae01-8ea9875cf9c3",
                                "sense_id": "2bdee422-0d20-3eca-9974-75d3afe4fca1",
                                "text": "Both chiral derivatives can be produced by making use of preexchange of the β positions of 2-oxoglutarate in ²H₂O."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16bf89eb-adaf-4bcc-bba3-8f18bad3b0a6",
                                "sense_id": "2bdee422-0d20-3eca-9974-75d3afe4fca1",
                                "text": "The advantage of this latter in-situ method is less time-consuming than the former because the intercalant does not have to be prepared separately, and no preexchange of the starting clay mineral is required."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "91ab7c00-ed41-3cee-ba59-c9e5a6bd638f",
                        "entry_id": "80457b3b-549f-3f0d-87c2-10d1415dcbb1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An interaction that introduces and leads to but is not yet a true exchange."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "62cfbded-7147-4453-9a27-ab77ce6f13c5",
                                "sense_id": "91ab7c00-ed41-3cee-ba59-c9e5a6bd638f",
                                "text": "This co-construction of reading turns is made to happen in a series of preexchanges (Kendon 1977) in which the girls lead each other to a conversational slot where a joint beginning of the reading is possible."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52c60ea5-7e01-43ca-8655-554707b15b9a",
                                "sense_id": "91ab7c00-ed41-3cee-ba59-c9e5a6bd638f",
                                "text": "The former group corresponds to Edmondson's preexchanges (1981); that is, initiation moves that focus to the speaker's assurance of fulfilment before making the request: (8) Can I ask you a question? (9) Could you do me a favour?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
